A||N||3||Elenor84||How do I get the throttle cable and cruise control off?||||1||
Z||000000||Elenor84||08-12-2001||07:36 AM||||Hey guys...doing a v6 swap!  I'm stuck on the cruise control cable and the throttle cable...how do I get them off of the throttle body?  Thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroSoul||08-12-2001||08:41 AM||||  It has been a while since I have done that but I am pretty sure they a both attached to the linkage with an E ring.  They also mount to a bracket with those squeeze and snap connectors (sorry don't know the proper technical name).  You have to squeeze the ears (another technical name)underneath the bracket and push them up from the bottom. Haynes manual has some mediocre pictures that help.  Look at removing the intake manifold.  Hope this helps.||||reg||6
Z||000002||KRMFiero||08-12-2001||09:48 AM||||I havent touched a Fiero engine in a few months so I cant remember whats holding them on, But My Caddy engine has a O with a little clip thingy comming down through the middle, it just pops off if you put a screw driver behind it.<P>Kyle||||reg||1
